        "original_id": "3d346864-6f31-54cb-8139-9d0f6c3b1a95",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Voltaire, Louis XIV of France, Charlemagne\n- Works: Essai sur les mœurs et l'esprit des nations\n- Places: Europe, the colonies, the East\n- Topics: universal history, European monarchy\n\nFacts:\n- In 1756, Voltaire first published Essai sur les mœurs et l'esprit des nations.\n- Essai sur les mœurs et l'esprit des nations is a work by the French writer, historian, and philosopher Voltaire.\n- Essai sur les mœurs et l'esprit des nations discusses the history of Europe from before Charlemagne to the dawn of the age of Louis XIV.\n- Essai sur les mœurs et l'esprit des nations also addresses the colonies and the East.\n- Louis XIV of France reigned for 72 years and 110 days.\n- Louis XIV of France has the longest recorded reign of any monarch of a sovereign country in European history.",
